APP_TITLE = "MaINbox v4.1.56 AI Assistant"  # v4.1.56: SENT-RFQ TRACKER + COVERAGE LOSS FIXES. Reported: an RFQ was sent, no Sent/Waiting tracker appeared, and no quote coverage was created. THREE root causes found; the first REPRODUCED exactly with the real functions. (1) WON-ORDER FALSE POSITIVE ON OUTBOUND REQUESTS: detect_won_order's weak inference (a PO number anywhere + a go-ahead word like release/ship/deliver) classified an outgoing RFQ such as "Please quote the attached list. Once approved we will release PO 1594-061 and need you to ship..." as a WON ORDER -> is_closed_ack -> the sent scan created NO tracker, NO coverage, and could even Complete the matching inbound row. Fix: detect_won_order gains outbound_request (keyword-only; other callers unchanged) which suppresses the two WEAK inferences (PO+go-ahead combo, bare good-to-go) when the outbound text explicitly ASKS -- for pricing (please quote / rfq / p&a / price and availability / need pricing / please provide) or for the counterparty's PO ("please send your PO 707 so we can release", which means the PO has NOT arrived). The strong explicit patterns (attached is the PO / release and deliver) still close even then, so real order releases are unaffected. (2) MIS-SLOTTED INTENT BLOCKED COVERAGE: even with a tracker, that RFQ wording fell through to Waiting on CUSTOMER (the generic PO-mention branch), and _auto_create_coverage_for_sent_rfq accepts ONLY Waiting-on-Vendor trackers -- coverage still refused. Fix: analyze_reply_intent decides outbound strong price-asks (please quote / rfq / p&a / price and availability / need pricing / need a quote / quote me) as Waiting on Vendor BEFORE the PO/order branch; deliberately narrow so an outbound "please send your PO..." still resolves Waiting on Customer. (3) SALES-MAILBOX SENDS WERE INVISIBLE: all sent-scan sites read ONLY GetDefaultFolder(5) (the user's own Sent Items); a message sent FROM the shared Sales mailbox is saved into THAT store's Sent Items and was never seen at all -- "it didn't even find it being sent". Fix: scan_recent_sent_waiting_trackers now walks BOTH folders via new _find_sales_sent_folder_in (worker-safe; locale-safe Store.GetDefaultFolder(5) with named-folder fallback; EntryID-deduped against My Sent), with PER-FOLDER fast-skip state (_sent_tracker_folder_state; the old single-folder skip returned early, which would have let an unchanged My Sent hide a new Sales send) and per-folder fault isolation (a broken Sales store can never break the user's own scan); the checked/max_items budget is per folder; the processed set, backfill, flush, and reconcile tail run once as before. Verified: 10-case intent matrix (the reported wording now yields tracker + Waiting on Vendor = coverage-eligible; genuine releases still close; inbound won/ack/ask behavior byte-equal in outcome; attachment-only RFQs still tracked) and structural proof of the folder loop (per-folder state, isolation, shared dedupe, single tail). No engine changes; AUTO_GROUP_ENGINE_MIN_VERSION stays 1.2.1, PO_MATCH_ENGINE_MIN_VERSION stays 1.8.3. v4.1.55: per-sender contact types + first-time save offer + Saved Employees. v4.1.54: sales-category ownership gate for coverage scans. (Full earlier changelog in git history.)
